2. Camoufox components
----------------------
CamoCrawl does not vendor Camoufox source code. It integrates with Camoufox
at runtime through:

- the `camoufox-js` npm client (https://github.com/apify/camoufox-js),
  licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0). A copy of that
  license is provided in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/camoufox-js-MPL-2.0.md; and
- the Camoufox browser build (https://github.com/daijro/camoufox), also
  MPL-2.0-licensed, which is downloaded at Docker build time
  (`camoufox-js fetch` in apps/playwright-service-ts/Dockerfile) and is not
  checked into this repository. Note that a small vendored part of the
  Camoufox browser (the `cursory` cursor-movement library,
  `additions/juggler/input/cursory/`) is licensed LGPLv3-or-later rather
  than MPL-2.0, per the upstream Camoufox repository.

No Camoufox source file has been copied into this repository, so no
Camoufox file-level header is reproduced here. The MPL-2.0 obligations that
apply are those of the `camoufox-js` dependency and of the browser binary
you download when building or running CamoCrawl; consult
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/README.md for details.

3. CamoCrawl-original code
--------------------------
The Camoufox rendering service in apps/playwright-service-ts
(camoufox.ts, config.ts, pool.ts, scrape.ts, ssrf.ts, logger.ts, the
corresponding *.spec.ts tests, and the rewrite of api.ts), together with the
associated Docker, Docker Compose, Helm, CI, and documentation changes, was
written for CamoCrawl. Like the Firecrawl code it builds on, it is made
available under the AGPL-3.0 terms in the root LICENSE file. Per-file
provenance headers are included in those sources.

